---
/**
 * AiGovernanceFigure — how a governed write actually works.
 *
 * A measured figure, not a product mock. It draws the three things that make
 * the assistant safe, all read from the source:
 *
 *   1. THE RISK LADDER — the tier a tool declares decides whether it may
 *      execute without asking. Read tools never confirm; low may auto-execute
 *      only if an administrator allows it; medium and above always ask.
 *   2. THE PREVIEW PAYLOAD — the exact keys the reservation previewer returns,
 *      including the phone masked by the privacy policy so raw contact never
 *      leaves the server unmasked.
 *   3. THE PENDING RECORD — `imbirt.ai.pending.action`, persisted rather than
 *      held in process memory, single-use via a conditional UPDATE, expiring
 *      after PENDING_ACTION_TTL_MINUTES.
 *
 * Sources: addons/imbirt_ai/models/ai_agent.py (risk tiers, previewer),
 * addons/imbirt_ai/models/ai_pending_action.py (record, TTL, `take()`).
 * Only the values are illustrative.
 *
 * Layout budget — keep these bands inside the viewBox:
 *   header   0–26    band 1  52–248    band 2  286–684
 *   band 3   724–1062                footer  1096–1134
 */

// Rendered as variables: a literal `{` inside an Astro template starts an
// expression, and a JSON sample is text, not an expression.
const argsSample = '{ "room_name": "204", "date_from": "2026-11-13", ... }';
const previewSample = '{ "kind": "reservation", "risk": "medium", ... }';
---

<figure class="governance-figure my-10">
  <div class="border border-rule bg-paper-raised p-4 shadow-plate sm:p-6">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 900 1160"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="gov-title gov-desc"
      class="block h-auto w-full"
      font-family="var(--font-body)"
    >
      <title id="gov-title">How a governed AI write works: the risk ladder, the preview payload, and the pending record</title>
      <desc id="gov-desc">
        First, a ladder of four risk tiers. Read never asks. Low may execute
        automatically only when an administrator has allowed it. Medium and
        above always require the user to confirm, and medium is the default for
        every write tool. Second, the preview payload the reservation tool
        returns: kind, risk, room, guest name, a masked phone number, check-in
        and check-out dates and a derived night count. Third, the pending action
        record that stores the write until it is confirmed, with its token,
        tool name, arguments, preview, state and fifteen minute expiry.
      </desc>

      <!-- hatching used to mark the one masked value -->
      <defs>
        <pattern id="gov-mask" width="6" height="6" patternTransform="rotate(45)" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="6" stroke="var(--brass-600)" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.35" />
        </pattern>
      </defs>

      <!-- ================= header ================= -->
      <text x="0" y="14" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="10" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.8">FIG. 07 — THE GOVERNED WRITE</text>
      <text x="900" y="14" text-anchor="end" fill="var(--ink-300)" font-size="9.5" letter-spacing="1.4">DRAWN FROM addons/imbirt_ai</text>
      <line x1="0" y1="26" x2="900" y2="26" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" />

      <!-- ================= band 1: the risk ladder ================= -->
      <g>
        <text x="0" y="52" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="10" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.6">1 · THE RISK LADDER</text>
        <text x="0" y="70" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">Every tool declares its own tier in its definition. The tier is not a policy applied afterwards.</text>

        <g transform="translate(0,84)">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="620" height="30" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="14" y="20" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="12" font-weight="600">read</text>
          <text x="120" y="20" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">never asks — a read is always free</text>

          <rect x="0" y="38" width="620" height="30" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="14" y="58" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="12" font-weight="600">low</text>
          <text x="120" y="58" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">may auto-execute — only if an administrator enabled the policy</text>

          <!-- the boundary -->
          <line x1="0" y1="80" x2="620" y2="80" stroke="var(--brass-600)" stroke-width="2" />
          <g stroke="var(--brass-600)" stroke-width="1">
            <line x1="0" y1="74" x2="0" y2="86" />
            <line x1="620" y1="74" x2="620" y2="86" />
          </g>

          <rect x="0" y="96" width="620" height="30" fill="var(--brass-200)" stroke="var(--brass-600)" />
          <text x="14" y="116" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="12" font-weight="700">medium</text>
          <text x="120" y="116" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">always asks — and this is the default for every write tool</text>

          <rect x="0" y="134" width="620" height="30" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="14" y="154" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="12" font-weight="600">high · critical</text>
          <text x="200" y="154" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11.5">reserved for destructive operations</text>

          <line x1="640" y1="0" x2="640" y2="164" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="664" y="24" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">THE BOUNDARY</text>
          <text x="664" y="46" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">Nothing at or below this line</text>
          <text x="664" y="62" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">reaches the database without</text>
          <text x="664" y="78" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">a human confirming it.</text>
          <text x="664" y="106" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="10.5">Read tools are declared</text>
          <text x="664" y="122" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="10.5">risk=read; write tools inherit</text>
          <text x="664" y="138" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="10.5">risk=medium unless they say</text>
          <text x="664" y="154" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="10.5">otherwise.</text>
        </g>
      </g>

      <!-- ================= band 2: the preview payload ================= -->
      <g transform="translate(0,286)">
        <text x="0" y="14" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="10" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.6">2 · THE PREVIEW PAYLOAD</text>
        <text x="0" y="32" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">What the tool assembles before anything is written. This object is echoed into the transcript and onto the confirmation.</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="46" x2="900" y2="46" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" />
        <text x="0" y="64" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">KEY</text>
        <text x="190" y="64" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">VALUE</text>
        <text x="470" y="64" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">WHY IT IS THERE</text>
        <line x1="0" y1="74" x2="900" y2="74" stroke="var(--rule)" />

        <line x1="0" y1="106" x2="900" y2="106" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="96" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">kind</text>
        <text x="190" y="96" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">"reservation"</text>
        <text x="470" y="96" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">the previewer's own discriminator</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="140" x2="900" y2="140" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="130" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">risk</text>
        <text x="190" y="130" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">"medium"</text>
        <text x="470" y="130" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">declared by the tool, so the card cannot downgrade itself</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="174" x2="900" y2="174" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="164" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">room</text>
        <text x="190" y="164" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">"204 — Deluxe King"</text>
        <text x="470" y="164" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">resolved against the real room record, not the user's wording</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="208" x2="900" y2="208" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="198" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">guest_name</text>
        <text x="190" y="198" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">"Mikael Tesfaye"</text>
        <text x="470" y="198" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">masked too, when the privacy policy requires it</text>

        <!-- the one masked value: hatched, so the masking is visible not merely claimed -->
        <line x1="0" y1="242" x2="900" y2="242" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <rect x="184" y="212" width="150" height="26" fill="url(#gov-mask)" />
        <text x="0" y="232" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">guest_phone</text>
        <text x="190" y="232" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">"+251 91****47"</text>
        <text x="470" y="232" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">masked in the preview — the raw number never leaves the server</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="276" x2="900" y2="276" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="266" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">date_from</text>
        <text x="190" y="266" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">"2026-11-13"</text>
        <text x="470" y="266" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">rejected outright if it falls in the past</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="310" x2="900" y2="310" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="300" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">date_to</text>
        <text x="190" y="300" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">"2026-11-16"</text>
        <text x="470" y="300" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">must fall after check-in, or the previewer refuses</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="344" x2="900" y2="344" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="334" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">nights</text>
        <text x="190" y="334" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11.5">3</text>
        <text x="470" y="334" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">derived, so the guest is never billed the wrong stay</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="378" x2="900" y2="378" stroke="var(--rule)" />
        <text x="0" y="368" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="11.5" font-family="monospace">summary</text>
        <text x="190" y="368" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">"New reservation for 204 — Deluxe King: Mikael Tesfaye,</text>
        <text x="190" y="384" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">2026-11-13 to 2026-11-16 (3 nights)"</text>
        <text x="470" y="368" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">the operator approves a sentence,</text>
        <text x="470" y="384" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">not a blob of JSON</text>
      </g>

      <!-- ================= band 3: the pending record ================= -->
      <g transform="translate(0,724)">
        <text x="0" y="14" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-size="10" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.6">3 · THE PENDING RECORD</text>
        <text x="0" y="32" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">Between the preview and the write, the intent lives in the database — not in process memory.</text>

        <line x1="0" y1="46" x2="900" y2="46" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" />
        <text x="0" y="64" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">FIELD</text>
        <text x="190" y="64" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">VALUE</text>
        <text x="470" y="64" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">WHAT IT GUARANTEES</text>
        <line x1="0" y1="74" x2="900" y2="74" stroke="var(--rule)" />

        <g font-size="11.5">
          <line x1="0" y1="106" x2="900" y2="106" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="0" y="96" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-family="monospace">_name</text>
          <text x="190" y="96" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-family="monospace">imbirt.ai.pending.action</text>
          <text x="470" y="96" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">a model, not a variable</text>

          <line x1="0" y1="132" x2="900" y2="132" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="0" y="122" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-family="monospace">token</text>
          <text x="190" y="122" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-family="monospace">9f2c4a...a41b</text>
          <text x="470" y="122" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">uuid4 hex, indexed, required</text>

          <line x1="0" y1="158" x2="900" y2="158" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="0" y="148" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-family="monospace">user_id</text>
          <text x="190" y="148" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-family="monospace">res.users(2)</text>
          <text x="470" y="148" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">the confirmation belongs to one person</text>

          <line x1="0" y1="184" x2="900" y2="184" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="0" y="174" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-family="monospace">tool_name</text>
          <text x="190" y="174" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-family="monospace">create_reservation</text>
          <text x="470" y="174" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">a stale token cannot run a different tool</text>

          <line x1="0" y1="210" x2="900" y2="210" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="0" y="200" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-family="monospace">args_json</text>
          <text x="190" y="200" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-family="monospace">{argsSample}</text>
          <text x="470" y="200" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">frozen at preview time</text>

          <line x1="0" y1="236" x2="900" y2="236" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="0" y="226" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-family="monospace">preview_json</text>
          <text x="190" y="226" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-family="monospace">{previewSample}</text>
          <text x="470" y="226" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">frozen at preview time</text>

          <line x1="0" y1="262" x2="900" y2="262" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="0" y="252" fill="var(--ink-900)" font-family="monospace">state</text>
          <text x="190" y="252" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-family="monospace">draft → consumed</text>
          <text x="470" y="252" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="11">the transition is what makes it single-use</text>
        </g>

        <!-- the two guarantees -->
        <g transform="translate(0,286)">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="438" height="86" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="16" y="24" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">PERSISTED</text>
          <text x="16" y="46" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">Stored in PostgreSQL, not in a Python process.</text>
          <text x="16" y="62" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">A confirmation survives a worker restart and</text>
          <text x="16" y="78" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">works across workers — the token is not bound</text>
          <text x="16" y="94" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">to the one that created it.</text>

          <rect x="462" y="0" width="438" height="86" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--rule)" />
          <text x="478" y="24" fill="var(--brass-600)" font-size="9.5" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="1.4">SINGLE USE</text>
          <text x="478" y="46" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">take() claims the row with a conditional UPDATE.</text>
          <text x="478" y="62" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">Two concurrent confirms race on the same row;</text>
          <text x="478" y="78" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">exactly one wins, and the other is told the</text>
          <text x="478" y="94" fill="var(--ink-700)" font-size="11">confirmation expired.</text>
        </g>
      </g>

      <!-- ================= footer ================= -->
      <line x1="0" y1="1096" x2="900" y2="1096" stroke="var(--rule-strong)" />
      <text x="0" y="1116" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.6">
        Field names, risk tiers, the masking rule and the fifteen-minute TTL are read from the source. The values are illustrative.
      </text>
      <text x="0" y="1132" fill="var(--ink-500)" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.6">
        No live capture exists: no LLM endpoint was available on the capture machine, and none is faked here.
      </text>
      <text x="0" y="1152" fill="var(--ink-300)" font-size="9.5" letter-spacing="1.4">
        PENDING_ACTION_TTL_MINUTES = 15 — THE SAME WINDOW GARBAGE-COLLECTS THE ROW
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</figure>
